Package: causalMed
Title: Parametric G-Formula for Longitudinal Mediation and Total Effects
Version: 0.1.4
Authors@R: c(person("Alimu", "Dayimu", 
                    email = "ad938@cam.ac.uk", 
                    role = c("aut", "cre"),
                    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-9998-7463")),
             person("Xingling", "Guo", 
                    role = c("aut")))
Description: Causal mediation analysis for longitudinal data with time-varying
    exposures, mediators and confounders, covering both interventional
    (Lin et al. (2017) <doi:10.1002/sim.7426>) and natural
    (Zheng and van der Laan (2017) <doi:10.1515/jci-2016-0006>) direct and
    indirect effects. Estimation uses the parametric g-formula
    (Robins (1986) <doi:10.1016/0270-0255(86)90088-6>), which is also exposed
    directly so that counterfactual means or risks can be estimated under
    static, dynamic or time-varying hypothetical interventions.
